  "text_md": "## <u>4. Charges other than tuition</u>\n\nApplication for coverage of fees other than tuition (i.e. Admissions, Transcripts, Parking, and Extended Education) must be sent to the appropriate department in order to prevent disruptions to student services\n\n## <u>5. Important Dates for the Winter 2018 Term</u>\n\nBelow are the important timelines that must be adhered to.\n\n|Description|Winter Term (Jan-April 2018)|\n|---|---|\n|Final Date for receipt of Sponsorship Applications without penalties|th 9 January 2018|\n|Final Date for receipt of Sponsorship Applications with penalties|th 10 February 2018|\n|Invoices Issued to Sponsors|th th 6 to 12 February 2018|\n|Invoice due date|All fees are due upon receipt of invoice|\n\nIf payment has not been made by the due date, you and your sponsor will be notified by email that payment has not been received. Following which your student account will be placed on hold and access to administrative services will be suspended and future term registration will not be permitted until the overdue balance has been paid in full.\n\n## <u>6. Penalties</u>\n\nSponsorship application received after the deadline of 9th January 2018, will result in an assessment of $50 late payment penalty to your Student account and further $40 late fee will be applied at the end of revision period if the Sponsorship application is not received.\n\nOnce the invoice is 30 days or more past due, the University reserves the right to deny any further credit to the sponsor, and overdue student account may be subject to regular collection processes.\n\nI hope this information is helpful, and if you require further information, please do not hesitate to contact me at the number below.\n\nSincerely,\n\nAbiola Idowu Receivables Analyst- (Sponsored Students) Abiola.idowu@umanitoba.ca 204-474-8718\n",
